==Strategy==
Everlord Wanwan is a [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] that is meant to be fought with all [[anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. For this reason, the battle becomes unnecessarily difficult without all superior quality treasures.

You have to be very mindful of Wanwan's Warp ability. His first two attacks do 15,000 damage each, followed by a 1,500-damage attack that Warps Cats for 66 seconds. With a deploy limit of 10 Cats, you can't afford to have very many Cats stuck in this Warp at once. Disposable units and Cats with Warp Immunity are obviously helpful, as they will deny him the opportunity to clog your cat limit. Other enemies might be quite the threat, and the victory condition is to outlast them so your units can hit Wanwan unobstructed.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]]: Due to how survive works, this unit will NOT get warped by Wanwan if he is on survive. One hit from Wanwan's damaging hits also puts him there so there is less risk of him taking up space compared to something like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]]
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime]]: Relic Doge and Wanwan himself are the only enemies with area attacks here, so you can use a well-timed Slime on certain enemies to generate a powerful wave attack that can snipe Wanwan and cripple peons, especially Relic Doges and Sir Rels.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]]: One of the best general attackers to use in this stage due to its low cost, high damage and Warp Immunity. While single attack limits its performance, it still works quite well and can be used to eliminate dangerous peons.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]]: Serves a similar purpose to Can Can, mostly used to get rid of peons like Sir Rel.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]]/[[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist]]: Deals massive damage to Red enemies and are used for countering Capy, the most threatening enemy in this stage. Courier is preferred due to having more range, long distance area attacks that hit Capy from behind, and can knockback Sir Rel in one hit at higher levels.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell]]: Due to its Warp Immunity and massive health for such a cheap unit, Green Shell is often abused in certain Uber-based cheese strategies that would be otherwise inconsistent. It also has its uses elsewhere, such as stalling Wanwan earlier on or to buy your units one extra second so they can kill a nasty Relic peon.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]: Can clean up Sir Rel, damage Wanwan, and deal with Mistress Celeboodle. Plus he dies to two Wanwan hits so there is lower risk of him taking up your space.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cutter]]: Deals massive damage to Red enemies, 100% chance to survive a lethal strike and strengthens by 400% at 1% health. If you manage to clear the other peons and Wanwan isn't stopping it anytime soon, you can use this to cripple a Capy. Cutter also has a damage combo with [[Li'l Axe Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Brave Cat]] which can make a tremendous difference when the right units are used.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]: A strong, quick attacker that can remove crazy amounts of health from Capy if timed right, although you can use him for better effect to get Wanwan off your base in case of an emergency, giving him a usage of being somewhat of a panic button.
*[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]]: Used to deal with Croconators and force Wanwan to attack in a pinch. It shouldn't survive Wanwan's hits, preventing it from clogging the cat limit.
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]: Can serve as your primary meatshield due to its Warp Immunity and unlike [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone]] it is slightly more consistent. It can also get rid of [[Those Guys]] on its own.
*Talented [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Bondage Cat]]: Being a Warp Immune tank, they serve well against Capy with the Dodge talent.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]]: Although he seems like he wouldn't work here, he can be used to temporarily disable the Relic Doges and Sir Rels, reducing their pushing power massively. Alternatively, he can be used like a more expensive Stone Cat, being able to act like an impassable barrier until his entire animation plays out, while his Surge can deal great chip damage to the boss.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]]: A unit with all the necessary abilities, those being Warp Immunity, Resistance and Massive Damage to Aliens, enough to melt the boss easily, especially with his Strengthen talent unlocked. However, he will have trouble hitting the boss due to the other peons getting in the way.
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]]: Another very good Pixie for this stage, with Warp Immunity, high HP, and a short cooldown ensuring you consistently have one on the field. Plus, their Waves can snipe Wanwan and get it to knockback many times. Just make sure they don't quickly get destroyed by Capy. They can also have Relic Targeting and Curse Immunity with talents, better dealing with the Relic Doges and Sir Rels.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Merc]]: Trixi works wonders here, as she can serve as a tanker, attacker and crowd-controller all in one. She has the health to easily tank Wanwan's first two attacks, and has Warp Immunity for his third hit, and can dish out great DPS to him when they're both alone. She can also basically disable the Relic peons, removing much of the threat they would otherwise pose. The only real threat to her here are the Capies, who will easily kill her thanks to her somewhat low range and lack of anti-Red abilities.

